# Both SQLite files are rebuildable and neither is versioned. market.db is 6.7M
# price rows straight from Yahoo; core.db is dominated by earnings_history,
# which Yahoo will also hand back on request.
#
# The one irreplaceable thing — the daily consensus snapshots, which cannot be
# re-fetched for a past date at any price — is committed as
# data/snapshots.csv.gz (127 KB and growing slowly), and core.db is rebuilt
# from it with `python db.py import`.
data/market.db
data/market.db-wal
data/market.db-shm
data/core.db
data/core.db-wal
data/core.db-shm
data/cache/
data/events.pkl
data/_run_*.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
results/scorecard.pkl

data/paper.db
data/paper.db-wal
data/paper.db-shm
